    "exact_target": "For every number field F, quasisplit connected reductive F-groups G-prime and G, and admissible L-homomorphism rho:L(G-prime)->L(G) (over Gamma_F, commuting with its projections, in Arthur Principle1.1's convention), every automorphic representation pi-prime of G-prime(A_F), in the inclusive Langlands sense cited there, has an automorphic representation pi of G(A_F) whose unramified Satake classes equal the images under rho_v of those of pi-prime outside a finite set of places. This is existence of a weak transfer, not uniqueness or a prescribed transfer function.",
