    "reader_question": "For arithmetic groups arising from simply connected, absolutely almost simple algebraic groups, is the congruence kernel\u2014the gap between finite-quotient and congruence information\u2014finite in total rank at least two when all selected nonarchimedean local ranks are positive, but infinite in rank one?",
    "why_it_matters": "The kernel measures the discrepancy between two ways of recovering an arithmetic group from finite information. A proof would classify that discrepancy as finite or infinite under these rank hypotheses, without requiring finite kernels to be trivial.",
