    "status_statement": "open_with_solved_subcases",
    "status_qualification": "Kahn's2024 final preprint retains Conjecture1 in general, distinguishes the known algebraic-triviality theorem and lists restricted cases. Bounded current discovery found no qualified full-scope positive or negative resolution; the newest discovered BB-related work concerns a different restricted target. This is not exhaustive claim-absence certification. Standing algebraic-closure and restricted-cycle hypotheses are retained, and Section11's diagonal-precomposed vanishing is not mistaken for full external nilpotence. The displayed status is retained from the selected, previously reviewed input, with its bound qualifications; no fresh current-status certification is claimed here.",
    "status_reviewed_at": null,
    "edition_date": "2026-09-22",
    "publication_id": "proofatlas.open-problem-ranking.top500.v22",
    "reader_question": "If an algebraic cycle with rational coefficients has zero intersection number against every complementary cycle, must multiplying copies of it on a product of sufficiently many copies of the variety make it zero modulo rational equivalence, for every smooth projective variety over any field?",
    "why_it_matters": "A proof would characterize numerical triviality by actual vanishing after enough external products. The required exponent may depend on the cycle, and the products take place on powers of the variety rather than within the original variety.",
