    "publication_id": "proofatlas.open-problem-ranking.top500.v22",
    "reader_question": "Can one choose d\u00b2 equally separated complex lines in every dimension d\u22652? Precisely, unit vectors along the lines must have the same squared overlap, |\u3008v,w\u3009|\u00b2=1/(d+1), for every distinct pair.",
