    "status_qualification": "Preserve the exact dated status attestations, evidence states, confidence and uncertainty flags; status remains open_with_solved_subcases. No public-cutoff, proof acceptance, recency-search or source-status upgrade is claimed. The literature varies between effective-cone, rational-hull, and relative formulations; this target fixes the absolute effective nef and movable statements for projective Q-factorial klt Calabi-Yau pairs over the complex numbers. Dimension two is proved, and many higher-dimensional geometric classes are known, but no source located through 2026-08-31 proves the stated general pair-level package. Historical attribution is layered: Morrison formulated the automorphism-cone form for Calabi-Yau varieties, Kawamata developed the minimal-model version, and later authors stated the klt-pair package used here. The displayed status is retained from the selected, previously reviewed input, with its bound qualifications; no fresh current-status certification is claimed here.",
