    "exact_target": "For every closed oriented three-manifold Y, let WRT_k(Y) be the SU(2) Witten-Reshetikhin-Turaev invariant at level k-2 in the standard compact-gauge normalization WRT_k(S^3)=1. For every value S in CS(Y), the set of Chern-Simons actions modulo Z of flat SU(2) connections, there should exist a formal Puiseux Laurent series W_S(tau) in union_{n>=1} C((tau^(1/n))) such that WRT_k(Y) ~ sum_{S in CS(Y)} exp(2*pi*i*k*S) W_S(1/k) as integer k tends to infinity, as a full Poincare asymptotic expansion. The separately named growth-rate and explicit leading-coefficient conjectures are not additional requirements.",
