      "exactTarget": "Determine the optimal fixed-blocklength reliability function of the memoryless binary symmetric channel without feedback for every crossover probability 0<p<1/2 and every rate 0<R<R_crit(p). With equiprobable messages, let P_e^*(n,R,p) be the minimum average block error under maximum-likelihood decoding among binary length-n codes of cardinality at least ceil(2^(nR)). Define E(R,p)=limsup_{n->infinity}[-log_2 P_e^*(n,R,p)]/n. Here H_2 is binary entropy and R_crit(p)=1-H_2(sqrt(p)/(sqrt(p)+sqrt(1-p))). Success requires matching achievable and converse exponents, or an equivalent evaluable exact characterization, for all these parameters. Restating the operational optimization or merely improving unmatched bounds is not a resolution.",
