    "exact_target": "Let L be the languages of binary strings decided by deterministic Turing machines using O(log(N+2)) work space on length-N inputs. Let RL use the same read-only input and read-write work-tape convention but allow fresh unbiased read-once random bits, retaining an old bit only by storing it in counted work space. The machine must halt for every input and every random tape, use O(log(N+2)) work space, accept each yes input with probability at least2/3, and accept each no input with probability0. Is every language in RL in L, equivalently RL=L?",
