    "publication_id": "proofatlas.open-problem-ranking.top500.v22",
    "reader_question": "Can majority\u2014whether at least half the input bits are one\u2014ever be computed by polynomial-size Boolean circuits with a fixed number of layers, using AND, OR, NOT and gates testing divisibility of their input count by one fixed modulus? The AND, OR and divisibility gates may take arbitrarily many inputs.",
