    "publication_id": "proofatlas.open-problem-ranking.top500.v22",
    "reader_question": "Polylogarithms are higher relatives of the logarithm. Can every number field's Dedekind zeta value at an integer at least two be expressed using a determinant of single-valued polylogarithms, multiplied by a nonzero rational number and the predicted factors involving \u03c0 and the field's discriminant?",
