    "domain_label": "Theoretical computer science",
    "exact_target": "Does there exist one deterministic algorithm A and constants C,c>0 such that, for every integer N>=2 given in unary, A outputs the adjacency matrix of a simple N-vertex graph in time at most O(N^c), with both its clique number and independence number at most C log_2 N? This is ordinary output-size polynomial explicitness, not poly(log N)-time adjacency queries.",
    "link": "https://arxiv.org/pdf/2103.05618v2",
