    "exact_target": "For every field K of arbitrary characteristic and every torsion-free group G, prove that each idempotent e in the ordinary scalar group ring K[G] is 0 or 1. Here K[G] consists of finite formal K-linear combinations of elements of G, with the group multiplication extended bilinearly, and idempotent means e^2=e. The group need not be finitely generated. This is not a claim that matrix rings over K[G], completed operator algebras or integral quandle rings have no nontrivial idempotents.",
