    "exact_target": "For each integer n>=2, let C_DFT(n) be the minimum number of steps needed to compute every output of the unnormalized complex DFT y_j=sum_(l=0)^(n-1) exp(-2*pi*i*j*l/n)x_l, 0<=j<n. Initially available functions are input coordinates and scalar constants; each step adds one affine function lambda*f+mu*g from two previously available functions with arbitrary complex scalars. Assertion: there exist c>0 and N such that C_DFT(n)>=c*n*log(n) for all n>=N. No coefficient bound, conditioning or memory restriction is imposed beyond this two-input scalar-step model.",
