    "exact_target": "Prove or disprove that every CAT(0) group satisfies the Tits alternative: if a discrete group G acts properly and cocompactly by isometries on a proper CAT(0) geodesic metric space, then every finitely generated subgroup H of G is either virtually solvable or contains a subgroup isomorphic to the free group F_2. Proper for the space means that closed bounded sets are compact; no geodesic-completeness, cube-complex or fixed-dimension hypothesis is imposed. Success is a proof for every such G and H, or a counterexample G,H violating both alternatives.",
