    "status_reviewed_at": null,
    "edition_date": "2026-09-22",
    "publication_id": "proofatlas.open-problem-ranking.top500.v22",
    "reader_question": "On a smooth complex projective Fano manifold, can curve counting and the organization of algebraic sheaves reveal the same structure? Dubrovin predicts that generic semisimplicity of quantum cohomology occurs exactly when the derived category of sheaves has a full exceptional collection, with compatible numerical data where the quantum product converges and is semisimple.",
    "why_it_matters": "A proof would connect quantum cohomology to categorical generation, with Stokes entries given by Euler pairings and the central connection matrix factored through modified Chern characters. The other factor must commute with cup product by c\u2081; the stronger Gamma-class formula is separate.",
