    "exact_target": "For every nonempty connected open domain Omega of the Riemann sphere, there exist a circle domain D in the Riemann sphere and a conformal homeomorphism Omega -> D. A circle domain means a nonempty connected open set each of whose complementary components is a closed round disk or a point. Allow arbitrary connectivity, including uncountably many complementary components and point components; the whole sphere (empty complement) and a sphere minus one point are included as trivial circle-domain cases. Conformal homeomorphism means a bijective conformal map, not a possibly noninjective holomorphic covering. No uniqueness, Mobius rigidity, quantitative distortion, explicit construction or boundary-extension requirement is appended. The universal statement is retained, not replaced by only an uncountable-connectivity or otherwise difficult subclass.",
