    "domain": "analysis_pde",
    "domain_label": "Analysis & PDE",
    "exact_target": "For every integer n>=2 and every finite integer m>=1, let f_1,...,f_m be scalar bounded holomorphic functions on the unit polydisc D^n={z in C^n: |z_k|<1 for all k}. If inf_{z in D^n} sum_{j=1}^m |f_j(z)|>0, then there exist scalar bounded holomorphic g_1,...,g_m on D^n such that sum_{j=1}^m f_j g_j=1 identically. No boundary extension, regularity, operator inequality or sharp solution-norm bound is required. Equivalently, for every n>=2, point evaluations from D^n are dense in the maximal ideal space of H-infinity(D^n).",
