    "exact_target": "For every integer n>=4, every lattice \u0393 in PU(n,1), the group of holomorphic isometries of complex hyperbolic n-space, is arithmetic. A lattice is a discrete subgroup of finite Haar covolume; both compact and noncompact finite-volume quotients and groups with torsion are included. Arithmeticity has its usual commensurability meaning via arithmetic subgroups of algebraic groups over Q projected through a compact-kernel real-group homomorphism, equivalently after the finite central lift to SU(n,1). No restriction to reflection lattices or one particular arithmetic construction is imposed. Here n is complex dimension, not real rank.",
