      "canonicalTitle": "NP-Hardness of Constant-Factor Approximation for Densest k-Subgraph",
      "exactTarget": "Let OPT(G,k)=max_{S subseteq V(G), |S|=k}|E(G[S])| for a finite simple undirected input graph G. Prove or refute the assertion that there exists an absolute constant epsilon>0 for which the promise problem of distinguishing OPT(G,k)>=t from OPT(G,k)<t/(1+epsilon), with input integers 1<=k<=|V(G)| and t>=1, is NP-hard under deterministic polynomial-time gap reductions. The target is any fixed nontrivial constant approximation gap for exactly k vertices, based on NP-hardness rather than a stronger average-case or exponential-time assumption.",
