    "domain_label": "Cryptography, coding, information & optimization",
    "exact_target": "For every finite undirected edge-capacitated network and every finite collection of independent source-destination unicast sessions, prove or disprove that the zero-error network-coding capacity region equals the fractional multicommodity-routing capacity region. Each undirected edge has a shared capacity bounding the sum of transmission rates in its two directions; intermediate nodes may causally encode received messages in the coding model. Fractional routing may split each session over paths. The target uses the standard zero-error formulation, not multicast or directed networks.",
