    "domain": "combinatorics_discrete_geometry",
    "domain_label": "Combinatorics & discrete geometry",
    "exact_target": "For all positive integers k,s,n with n>=ks, let F be a family of distinct k-element subsets of [n]={1,...,n} containing no s pairwise disjoint members. The conjecture asserts |F|<=max{binom(ks-1,k), binom(n,k)-binom(n-s+1,k)}. Here binom(a,k)=0 for integers 0<=a<k. For s=1 the family is empty, and k=1 is included as a trivial case. The two terms are attained by all k-subsets of a fixed (ks-1)-set and by all k-subsets meeting a fixed (s-1)-set, respectively. Their role is sharpness of the bound, not an additional classification of all equality families.",
